-- ccc23-fitness.l4 -- sections 672.22 to 672.33 (Fitness to Stand Trial) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Form: see the header of ccc23-assessment.l4. The s 2 answer "unfit to stand trial" is a seam input `by s 2 unfit to stand trial` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, as PLAN.md section 4 names it).

§ `Section 672.22 -- Presumption of fitness`

-- 672.22: an accused is presumed fit to stand trial unless the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial.
-- src:13429 | 672.22 An accused is presumed fit to stand trial unless the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial.
@ref s 672.22 (src:13429)
GIVEN `the accused is unfit to stand trial, by s 2 unfit to stand trial` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.22 the accused is presumed fit to stand trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial` AND `the accused is unfit to stand trial, by s 2 unfit to stand trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial"
        IF `the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial` AND `the accused is unfit to stand trial, by s 2 unfit to stand trial` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "unfit to stand trial"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 672.23 and 672.24 -- Trying the issue; counsel`

-- 672.23(1): where the court has reasonable grounds, at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered, to believe that the accused is unfit to stand trial, the court may direct, of its own motion or on application of the accused or the prosecutor, that the issue of fitness be tried.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13431 | 672.23 (1) Where the court has reasonable grounds, at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered, to believe that the accused is unfit to stand trial, the court may direct, of its own motion or on application of the accused or the prosecutor, that the issue of fitness of the accused be tried.
@ref s 672.23(1) (src:13431)
GIVEN `the court has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court acts of its own motion, or on application of the accused or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.23(1) the court may direct that the issue of fitness be tried` MEANS
    IF `the court has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is unfit to stand trial` AND `it is a stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered` AND `the court acts of its own motion, or on application of the accused or the prosecutor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court has reasonable grounds, at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered, to believe that the accused is unfit to stand trial"

-- 672.23(2): an accused or a prosecutor who makes an application under subsection (1) has the burden of proof that the accused is unfit to stand trial. Where the court acts of its own motion the text names no one who bears it.
-- src:13433 | (2) An accused or a prosecutor who makes an application under subsection (1) has the burden of proof that the accused is unfit to stand trial.
@ref s 672.23(2) (src:13433)
GIVEN `the accused or the prosecutor makes an application under subsection 672.23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.23(2) the applicant has the burden of proof that the accused is unfit to stand trial` MEANS
    IF `the accused or the prosecutor makes an application under subsection 672.23(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "An accused or a prosecutor who makes an application under subsection (1) has the burden of proof"

-- 672.24(1): where the court has reasonable grounds to believe that an accused is unfit to stand trial and the accused is not represented by counsel, the court shall order that the accused be represented by counsel.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13435 | 672.24 (1) Where the court has reasonable grounds to believe that an accused is unfit to stand trial and the accused is not represented by counsel, the court shall order that the accused be represented by counsel.
@ref s 672.24(1) (src:13435)
GIVEN `the court has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.24(1) the court must order that the accused be represented by counsel` MEANS
    IF `the court has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is unfit to stand trial` AND NOT `the accused is represented by counsel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court has reasonable grounds to believe that an accused is unfit to stand trial and the accused is not represented by counsel"

-- 672.24(2): where counsel is assigned pursuant to (1) and legal aid is not granted pursuant to a provincial legal aid program, the fees and disbursements of counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General to the extent that the accused is unable to pay them.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13437 | (2) Where counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (1) and legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program, the fees and disbursements of counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General to the extent that the accused is unable to pay them.
@ref s 672.24(2) (src:13437)
GIVEN `counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection 672.24(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legal aid is granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.24(2) the Attorney General must pay the fees and disbursements of counsel` MEANS
    IF `counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection 672.24(1)` AND NOT `legal aid is granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (1) and legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program"

-- The amount: "to the extent that the accused is unable to pay them". The Attorney General pays the part of the fees and disbursements that the accused cannot pay. The figures are inputs.
@ref s 672.24(2) (src:13437)
GIVEN `the fees and disbursements of counsel, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that the accused is able to pay, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the Attorney General must pay, by s 672.24(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 672.24(2) the amount the Attorney General must pay, in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Attorney General must pay, by s 672.24(2)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (IF `the fees and disbursements of counsel, in dollars` MINUS `the amount that the accused is able to pay, in dollars` AT LEAST 0 THEN `the fees and disbursements of counsel, in dollars` MINUS `the amount that the accused is able to pay, in dollars` ELSE 0)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states no payment where it does not apply
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection 672.24(2) is carried through

