§ `Sections 672.25 to 672.27 -- Postponing, and who tries the issue`

-- 672.25(1): the court shall postpone directing the trial of the issue of fitness of an accused in proceedings for an offence for which the accused may be prosecuted by indictment or that is punishable on summary conviction,
-- until the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of indictment or summary conviction. The "until" is the text's own limit: once the prosecutor has elected, the duty to postpone is over (JUST FALSE).
-- src:13441 | 672.25 (1) The court shall postpone directing the trial of the issue of fitness of an accused in proceedings for an offence for which the accused may be prosecuted by indictment or that is punishable on summary conviction, until the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of indictment or summary conviction.
@ref s 672.25(1) (src:13441)
GIVEN `the offence is one for which the accused may be prosecuted by indictment or that is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of indictment or summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.25(1) the court must postpone directing the trial of the issue of fitness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is one for which the accused may be prosecuted by indictment or that is punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence for which the accused may be prosecuted by indictment or that is punishable on summary conviction"
        IF `the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of indictment or summary conviction` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of indictment or summary conviction"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 672.25(2): the court may postpone directing the trial of the issue of fitness (a) where the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at a preliminary inquiry, until a time not later than the time the accused is called on to answer to the charge;
-- or (b) where the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at trial, until a time not later than the opening of the case for the defence or, on motion of the accused, any later time that the court may direct.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13443 | (2) The court may postpone directing the trial of the issue of fitness of an accused
-- src:13444 | (a) where the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at a preliminary inquiry, until a time that is not later than the time the accused is called on to answer to the charge; or
-- src:13445 | (b) where the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at trial, until a time not later than the opening of the case for the defence or, on motion of the accused, any later time that the court may direct.
@ref s 672.25(2); s 672.25(2)(a); s 672.25(2)(b) (src:13443-13445)
GIVEN `the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at trial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.25(2) the court may postpone directing the trial of the issue of fitness` MEANS
    IF `the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at a preliminary inquiry` OR `the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution at trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the issue arises before the close of the case for the prosecution"

-- The time to which the trial of the issue may be postponed under 672.25(2): (a) at a preliminary inquiry, not later than the time the accused is called on to answer to the charge; (b) at trial, not later than the opening of the case for the defence,
-- or, on motion of the accused, any later time that the court may direct.
@ref s 672.25(2)(a); s 672.25(2)(b) (src:13444-13445)
GIVEN `the issue arose at a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the postponement is until a time not later than the time the accused is called on to answer to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue arose at trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the postponement is until a time not later than the opening of the case for the defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on motion of the accused the court directs a later time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.25(2) the postponement is within the time the paragraph allows` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the issue arose at a preliminary inquiry` THEN (IF `the postponement is until a time not later than the time the accused is called on to answer to the charge` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until a time that is not later than the time the accused is called on to answer to the charge"
        IF `the issue arose at trial` THEN (IF `the postponement is until a time not later than the opening of the case for the defence` OR `on motion of the accused the court directs a later time` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until a time not later than the opening of the case for the defence or, on motion of the accused, any later time that the court may direct"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraphs speak only of an issue arising at a preliminary inquiry or at trial

-- 672.26: where an accused is tried or is to be tried before a court composed of a judge and jury, (a) if the judge directs that the issue of fitness be tried before the accused is given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment, a jury of the number
-- required for the indictment in the province shall be sworn to try that issue and, with the consent of the accused, the issues to be tried on the indictment; and (b) if after, the jury shall be sworn to try that issue in addition to the issues for which it is already sworn.
-- src:13447 | 672.26 Where an accused is tried or is to be tried before a court composed of a judge and jury,
-- src:13448 | (a) if the judge directs that the issue of fitness of the accused be tried before the accused is given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment, a jury composed of the number of jurors required in respect of the indictment in the province where the trial is to be held shall be sworn to try that issue and, with the consent of the accused, the issues to be tried on the indictment; and
-- src:13449 | (b) if the judge directs that the issue of fitness of the accused be tried after the accused has been given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment, the jury shall be sworn to try that issue in addition to the issues in respect of which it is already sworn.
@ref s 672.26; s 672.26(a); s 672.26(b) (src:13447-13449)
DECLARE `s 672.26 jury sworn` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.26 a jury of the number required for the indictment is sworn to try the issue of fitness`
    `s 672.26 a jury of the number required for the indictment is sworn to try the issue of fitness and, with the consent of the accused, the issues to be tried on the indictment`
    `s 672.26 the jury is sworn to try the issue of fitness in addition to the issues in respect of which it is already sworn`
    `s 672.26 not covered`

@ref s 672.26; s 672.26(a); s 672.26(b) (src:13447-13449)
GIVEN `the accused is tried or is to be tried before a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge directs that the issue of fitness be tried before the accused is given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the judge directs that the issue of fitness be tried after the accused has been given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the accused consents that the issues on the indictment be tried by the jury sworn to try the issue of fitness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 672.26 jury sworn`
`s 672.26 how the jury is sworn` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is tried or is to be tried before a court composed of a judge and jury` THEN `s 672.26 not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an accused is tried or is to be tried before a court composed of a judge and jury"
        IF `the judge directs that the issue of fitness be tried before the accused is given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment` AND `the accused consents that the issues on the indictment be tried by the jury sworn to try the issue of fitness` THEN `s 672.26 a jury of the number required for the indictment is sworn to try the issue of fitness and, with the consent of the accused, the issues to be tried on the indictment`
        IF `the judge directs that the issue of fitness be tried before the accused is given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment` THEN `s 672.26 a jury of the number required for the indictment is sworn to try the issue of fitness`
        IF `the judge directs that the issue of fitness be tried after the accused has been given in charge to a jury for trial on the indictment` THEN `s 672.26 the jury is sworn to try the issue of fitness in addition to the issues in respect of which it is already sworn`
        OTHERWISE `s 672.26 not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the judge has not directed that the issue be tried

