§ `Sections 672.28 to 672.32 -- Verdicts on the issue and their effect`

-- 672.28: where the verdict on trial of the issue is that an accused is fit to stand trial, the arraignment, preliminary inquiry, trial or other stage of the proceeding shall continue as if the issue of fitness had never arisen.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
