§ `Section 672.33 -- Prima facie case to be made every two years`

-- 672.33(1): the court that has jurisdiction in respect of the offence charged against an accused who is found unfit to stand trial shall hold an inquiry, not later than two years after the verdict is rendered and every two years thereafter
-- until the accused is acquitted pursuant to subsection (6) or tried, to decide whether sufficient evidence can be adduced at that time to put the accused on trial. As a regulative rule: the court's duty, within the days to the day two years after the verdict.
-- src:13467 | 672.33 (1) The court that has jurisdiction in respect of the offence charged against an accused who is found unfit to stand trial shall hold an inquiry, not later than two years after the verdict is rendered and every two years thereafter until the accused is acquitted pursuant to subsection (6) or tried, to decide whether sufficient evidence can be adduced at that time to put the accused on trial.
@ref s 672.33(1) (src:13467)
DECLARE `s 672.33(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.33(1) hold an inquiry to decide whether sufficient evidence can be adduced to put the accused on trial`

GIVEN `the day the verdict is rendered, or the day the last inquiry was held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 672.33(1) act`
`s 672.33(1) the court must hold an inquiry` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 672.33(1) hold an inquiry to decide whether sufficient evidence can be adduced to put the accused on trial`
    WITHIN (Day (`add years` `the day the verdict is rendered, or the day the last inquiry was held` 2) MINUS Day `the day the verdict is rendered, or the day the last inquiry was held`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "no inquiry was held within two years after the verdict or the last inquiry"

-- The same duty as a decision function over dates (the extension of subsection (1.1) is an input). JUST TRUE if held not later than two years after the verdict (or the last inquiry), or within an extension; JUST FALSE otherwise.
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
