      `the day the inquiry is held` IS A DATE
      `the court has extended the period under subsection 672.33(1.1) to` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.33(1) the inquiry is held not later than two years after the verdict or the last inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the day the inquiry is held` AT MOST (`add years` `the day the verdict is rendered, or the day the last inquiry was held` 2)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the court has extended the period under subsection 672.33(1.1) to`
         WHEN JUST extended THEN (IF `the day the inquiry is held` AT MOST extended THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than two years after the verdict is rendered and every two years thereafter"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than two years after the verdict is rendered and every two years thereafter"

-- 672.33(1.1): despite (1), the court may extend the period for holding an inquiry where it is satisfied on the basis of an application by the prosecutor or the accused that the extension is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13469 | (1.1) Despite subsection (1), the court may extend the period for holding an inquiry where it is satisfied on the basis of an application by the prosecutor or the accused that the extension is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 672.33(1.1) (src:13469)
GIVEN `the prosecutor or the accused applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied on the basis of the application that the extension is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.33(1.1) the court may extend the period for holding an inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor or the accused applies` AND `the court is satisfied on the basis of the application that the extension is necessary for the proper administration of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it is satisfied on the basis of an application by the prosecutor or the accused that the extension is necessary for the proper administration of justice"

-- 672.33(2): on application of the accused, the court may order an inquiry under this section to be held at any time if it is satisfied, on the basis of the application and any written material submitted by the accused, that there is reason to doubt that there is a prima facie case against the accused.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:13471 | (2) On application of the accused, the court may order an inquiry under this section to be held at any time if it is satisfied, on the basis of the application and any written material submitted by the accused, that there is reason to doubt that there is a prima facie case against the accused.
@ref s 672.33(2) (src:13471)
GIVEN `the accused applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied, on the basis of the application and any written material submitted by the accused, that there is reason to doubt that there is a prima facie case against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.33(2) the court may order an inquiry to be held at any time` MEANS
    IF `the accused applies` AND `the court is satisfied, on the basis of the application and any written material submitted by the accused, that there is reason to doubt that there is a prima facie case against the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is satisfied, on the basis of the application and any written material submitted by the accused"

-- 672.33(3): at an inquiry under this section, the burden of proof that sufficient evidence can be adduced to put the accused on trial is on the prosecutor.
-- src:13473 | (3) At an inquiry under this section, the burden of proof that sufficient evidence can be adduced to put the accused on trial is on the prosecutor.
@ref s 672.33(3) (src:13473)
GIVEN `it is an inquiry under section 672.33` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.33(3) the prosecutor has the burden of proof that sufficient evidence can be adduced to put the accused on trial` MEANS
    IF `it is an inquiry under section 672.33`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At an inquiry under this section"

-- 672.33(4): in an inquiry under this section, the court shall admit as evidence (a) any affidavit containing evidence that would be admissible if given by the person making the affidavit as a witness in court; or (b) any certified copy of the oral testimony given at a previous inquiry or hearing before a court in respect of the offence charged.
-- src:13475 | (4) In an inquiry under this section, the court shall admit as evidence
-- src:13476 | (a) any affidavit containing evidence that would be admissible if given by the person making the affidavit as a witness in court; or
-- src:13477 | (b) any certified copy of the oral testimony given at a previous inquiry or hearing held before a court in respect of the offence with which the accused is charged.
@ref s 672.33(4); s 672.33(4)(a); s 672.33(4)(b) (src:13475-13477)
GIVEN `it is an affidavit containing evidence that would be admissible if given by the person making the affidavit as a witness in court` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it is a certified copy of the oral testimony given at a previous inquiry or hearing held before a court in respect of the offence with which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.33(4) the court must admit it as evidence at the inquiry` MEANS
    IF `it is an affidavit containing evidence that would be admissible if given by the person making the affidavit as a witness in court` OR `it is a certified copy of the oral testimony given at a previous inquiry or hearing held before a court in respect of the offence with which the accused is charged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the court shall admit as evidence"

-- 672.33(5): the court may determine the manner in which an inquiry under this section is conducted and may follow the practices and procedures in respect of a preliminary inquiry under Part XVIII where it concludes that the interests of justice so require.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13479 | (5) The court may determine the manner in which an inquiry under this section is conducted and may follow the practices and procedures in respect of a preliminary inquiry under Part XVIII where it concludes that the interests of justice so require.
@ref s 672.33(5) (src:13479)
GIVEN `it is an inquiry under section 672.33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court concludes that the interests of justice so require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.33(5) the court may follow the practices and procedures of a preliminary inquiry under Part XVIII` MEANS
    IF `it is an inquiry under section 672.33` AND `the court concludes that the interests of justice so require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it concludes that the interests of justice so require"

-- 672.33(6): where, on the completion of an inquiry under this section, the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence cannot be adduced to put the accused on trial, the court shall acquit the accused.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13481 | (6) Where, on the completion of an inquiry under this section, the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence cannot be adduced to put the accused on trial, the court shall acquit the accused.
@ref s 672.33(6) (src:13481)
GIVEN `the inquiry under section 672.33 is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence cannot be adduced to put the accused on trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.33(6) the court must acquit the accused` MEANS
    IF `the inquiry under section 672.33 is complete` AND `the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence cannot be adduced to put the accused on trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on the completion of an inquiry under this section, the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence cannot be adduced to put the accused on trial"
